      "updated_at": "2026-07-29T16:47:00Z",
      "body": "**Gate C fixture price, disclosed (era-note re-pin in the last commit).** The regression gate correctly caught the deliberate #281 semantics change on the CI fixture corpus: top-1 0.317→0.300 (−1.7pp, within the 2pp threshold) and WB 9.86→10.2357 (+0.3757, over the 0.1 threshold — hence the re-pin, thresholds unchanged). On D3 — the scale the #244 decision was made at — the price is ±0.0pp top-1 and +0.087 WB at 2.56× fewer keys. The fixture's 150-story miniature dilutes sparse merged evidence harder than the real corpus; if the team weighs the fixture signal differently, the revert is a one-function swap (build_store_multi + primary-key predicts). Automerge stays armed; CI reruns on the re-pin commit.",
